course: dictionary
lesson: 4430
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around the word, which is its context. Handball is a good example.
explain: «A handball goal» appears in a sentence about cheating and breaking the rules. Here handball is a foul in football, when a player touches the ball with a hand or arm. The clues are cheating, break the rules and goal.
explain: Handball can also be a team game of throwing and passing a ball, or a playground game. Ask: what is the sentence about? «Popular sports in France include football, rugby, tennis, cycling, handball and judo» is a list of sports, so handball means the game.
fact: Handball means a team game in which players throw and pass a ball with their hands and try to throw it into the other team's goal.
fact: In football, a handball is a foul when a player other than the goalkeeper touches the ball with a hand or arm.
fact: In some places, handball is a playground game of hitting a ball against a wall or into squares with the hand. It is also called «downball» or «four square».
fact: Handball is an Olympic sport, and it teaches passing, catching and teamwork in PE lessons.
fact: In Australian football, a handball is a way of passing by punching the ball from your hand.
exercise: «Cheating isn't only drugs: a handball goal, sandpaper on a cricket ball or a hidden motor in a bike all break the rules.» In this sentence, what is a handball? | A playground game played on a grass field with bats | *A foul in football when a player touches the ball with a hand or arm | A pass made by kicking the ball along the ground | A team game played on a court with a net
exercise: In PE, Miss Hart says, «Today we play handball to practise passing and catching.» Which meaning is this? | A foul in football | A way of passing in Australian football by punching the ball | *The team game of throwing and passing a ball into a goal | A rule about the goalkeeper catching the ball
exercise: At a football match, Sam hears the referee shout, «Handball!» What has happened? | *A player touched the ball with a hand or arm | The ball went out over the line | The goalkeeper caught the ball | A player scored a goal with the head
test: «Popular sports in France include football, rugby, tennis, cycling, handball and judo.» What does handball mean in this sentence? | A foul when a player touches the ball with a hand | A kind of goal | A playground game of hitting a ball against a wall | *The team game of throwing and passing a ball into a goal
test: In Australian schools, pupils play handball in painted squares at break time. What kind of game is it? | A pass made by kicking the ball | *A playground game of hitting a ball into squares with the hand | A team game with a net and a racket | A foul in football
exam: Which word in «Cheating isn't only drugs: a handball goal, sandpaper on a cricket ball or a hidden motor in a bike all break the rules» tells you handball is against the rules? | *cheating | bike | cricket | sandpaper
